{"id": "EUVD-2026-108719", "enisaUuid": "cad4e73d-32c0-3d67-8577-f019c2a48efd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nf_conntrack_expect: zero at allocation time\n\nThere are occasional LLM hints wrt. leaking uninitialized data to\nuserspace via ctnetlink.  Just zero at allocation time,\nexpectations are not frequently used these days.\n\nIntentionally keeps _init as-is because we could theoretically\nsupport re-init, so add the missing exp->dir there.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39cb6ff947c16a576ea68c5f272e634acdcb0085", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90545aa07a183887e9d72ce573c18e08f62e2c91", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c11d7ea5ff4dbe162e79f00188814ef5483c295", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7f3ee925aee9f1f547d539bc03c35433c238958", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/824397af7bfe14edad374c64253dae0187ca623d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a39ecb856514274c80d0fac4d128dba6b266a8ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/241ccd2fed9051db443aadce248fc0ab30f55e97"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98873"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19edd8bf-8ba4-39a0-b0e2-f9ee5b84f4c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "22b76dc4-1b35-36d1-9037-47a012b9ee0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.1.189"}, {"id": "277b0989-817a-35ad-af2d-8ea612a48584", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "305c48ee-5a6a-3967-a4aa-88fc89b1f21b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "3581f023-fd07-31e6-b776-a9b42bf38ad7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <241ccd2fed